{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":114684,"duration_api_ms":114650,"num_turns":13,"result":"","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"31e35406-1118-49be-a010-0ebc67b0647b","total_cost_usd":0.49127675,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":38213,"cache_read_input_tokens":214921,"output_tokens":5798,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":38213,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":7,"outputTokens":5798,"cacheReadInputTokens":214921,"cacheCreationInputTokens":38213,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.49127675,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"summary":"Accept the two test-robustness and observability improvements (positive-control assertion on cool arm, structured traces for summary runs). Reject the rest: DOC/DON absolute values are intentional per reproduction_factors.rs comment, cycle counting works correctly under emit_once_per_day dedup, bicarbonate is solver-derived so the alkalinity mismatch is harmless, and per-stage trace enhancement is a feature request beyond what's needed.","votes":[{"amendment_id":"fr-3-e17508b1","decision":"reject","rationale":"The identical DOC=5.0 / DON=0.8 pattern without `* vol` appears in reproduction_factors.rs:35-36 with an explicit comment: \"Keep DOC/DON low to avoid transient ammonia spike from mineralization.\" This is deliberately low to prevent mineralization from producing ammonia in breeding fixtures where clean chemistry (ammonia ≈ 0) is critical. The absolute values are an intentional choice, not a copy-paste bug."},{"amendment_id":"fr-3-56785ca4","decision":"reject","rationale":"The `emit_once_per_day` deduplication means each simulated day produces at most one ShrimpBerried and one ShrimpHatched event entry. The BTreeSet of unique days therefore counts the same thing the event log entries would count. Pairing berried-to-hatch by temporal ordering adds complexity without changing the result under the current event model, and the ≥2 threshold is already a generous lower bound. No demonstrated bug."},{"amendment_id":"fr-3-70ade949","decision":"reject","rationale":"The WaterState default (water.rs:104) documents bicarbonate as 'solver-derived; set by resolve_carbonate_state below', meaning the carbonate equilibrium solver uses DIC and alkalinity to derive bicarbonate and pH. The cached bicarbonate_mg_total set in the fixture is overwritten by the solver. The alkalinity/bicarbonate mismatch therefore has no effect on pH calculation. A clarifying comment could be added but there is no functional defect."},{"amendment_id":"fr-3-f6292b8a","decision":"accept","rationale":"The test currently checks cool-arm health (condition, molt stress) but never asserts that the cool arm actually breeds. A regression that suppresses breeding in both arms passes as long as the warm arm is slightly worse. Adding a positive-control breeding assertion (e.g. juveniles > 0, or minimum berried events, or a readiness floor) on the cool arm closes this gap and makes the thermal suppression probe genuinely differential rather than vacuously satisfied when both arms fail."},{"amendment_id":"fr-3-94619e54","decision":"accept","rationale":"enable_probe_instrumentation() attaches a SimTracer with Verbosity::Trace, but finish() discards traces for successful runs unless TANK_E2E_VERBOSE=1. For the summary workflow that aggregates multiple probes, this means successful executions produce no persisted trace output, limiting reproducibility and post-hoc analysis. Writing a JSONL sink or trace bundle for successful summary runs is a concrete observability improvement with clear value for scientific simulation workflows."},{"amendment_id":"fr-3-b144e01e","decision":"reject","rationale":"While the tracer does record only aggregate condition/reserve (not per-stage), it already records per-stage counts, and the shrimp_diag() function dumps full per-stage diagnostics into failure messages. Between the per-tick trace (counts + aggregate metrics), failure-message diagnostics, and checkpoint snapshots, there is sufficient data for debugging. Adding per-stage condition/reserve fields to the tracer and snapshot is a feature enhancement that adds schema complexity without addressing a blocking diagnostic gap."}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"4ffc8181-feb4-4018-8ae4-a9779d73840f"}
